e pauses are required by the grammar of Lojban, and {na.e} takes one less c=
haracter than {na .e}. Furthermore, not having the space serves to visually=
 group the words together, subtly signalling to readers that the two words =
are linked. With {na.e}, for example, the {na} modifies the {.e}, and in fa=
ct, the {na} makes no sense without the {.e}, and the {.e} means something =
else entirely without the {na}.<br>



<br>A .e B =3D A and B: "1 .e 1" =3D 1<br>A na.e B =3D !A and B, (not A) an=
d B: "1 na.e 1" =3D "0 .e 1" =3D 0<br>A .enai B =3D A and !B, A and (not B)=
: "1 .enai 1" =3D "1 .e 0" =3D 0<br>


